      "short": "The scatter plot shows a strong positive linear association: as Test 1 scores increase, Test 2 scores generally increase.",
      "worked": "Use Test 1 on the horizontal axis and Test 2 on the vertical axis. Plot the nine ordered pairs:\n\n$(214,216)$, $(281,270)$, $(212,221)$, $(324,326)$, $(340,330)$, $(205,207)$, $(208,213)$, $(304,312)$ and $(303,311)$.\n\nThe points lie close to an increasing straight-line trend. Students who score higher on Test 1 generally also score higher on Test 2, showing a strong positive linear association.",
